---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms of use | RentalSpy" description="Terms of use for RentalSpy.">
  <Prose title="Terms of use">
    <p class="lede">Plain-English terms. By using RentalSpy you agree to them.</p>
    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>RentalSpy is a free website that shows public rental and crime data and what renters share about places they've lived. It's provided as is. Government figures are medians for a whole suburb and can be out of date; renter entries are personal opinions and experiences. Always inspect a place and read your lease before signing.</p>
    <h2>You must be 18 or older to post</h2>
    <h2>When you post</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You confirm it's your own honest experience and follows the <a href="/rules/">rules</a>.</li>
      <li>You're responsible for what you post. Don't post anything untrue, or anything about a person.</li>
      <li>You let RentalSpy show your entry (without your identity) on the site, and use it in anonymous totals and averages.</li>
      <li>You can delete your entries any time on <a href="/me/">My places</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What we can do</h2>
    <p>We can refuse, hide or remove any entry, and block accounts that break the rules or misuse the site, including automated or bulk use.</p>
    <h2>Problems and complaints</h2>
    <p>If you think something on RentalSpy is untrue or harmful, use <a href="/report-a-problem/">Report a problem</a>. We review complaints quickly and will hide content while we look at it.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, RentalSpy isn't liable for decisions you make using the site. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under the Australian Consumer Law.</p>
    <p class="note">These terms are governed by the laws of South Australia.</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
